_model: definition
---
title: Definition 10
---
order: 10
---
short_label: III.Def.10
---
statement: A <i>sector</i> of a circle is the figure which, when an angle is constructed at the center of the circle, is contained by the straight lines containing the angle and the circumference cut off by them.
---
guide:

<figure class="diagram rdiagram">
<canvas id="canvas_1" width="300" height="240" tabindex="0"></canvas>
